<urn:usf:rule:completion-check-receipts-execution-intent:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Before any new canonical check effect, while holding the existing candidate lock, authenticate the current candidate, validation and execution authority. Derive exact execution input and intent identities from those values, not caller data. Create a contained owner-only no-follow PREPARED intent atomically and fsync its file and parent directory; atomically persist and fsync STARTED before child spawn. Refuse unsafe or conflicting pending intent publication without deleting bytes. On every native entry, including legacy explicit execution, inspect retained intent before scratch reset or invocation. A current matching final receipt may reconcile STARTED or SETTLED without execution; STARTED without an authenticated receipt becomes UNKNOWN and refuses redispatch. UNKNOWN remains blocked without an independently authenticated outcome readback. PREPARED is pre-effect only. Persist SETTLED only after current matching receipt readback, with its exact digest. Do not invent historical intents for current retained receipts. Legacy explicit behavior is unchanged when no intent exists. Required schema fields and state enumeration must agree exactly with current semantic requiredField and allowedState declarations before interpretation. Preserve scalar checked-receipt schema, digest domain, native locks and confinement. Intent records are recovery state, never semantic completion or telemetry authority." <urn:usf:graph:check-execution-intent> .
